From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 14:59:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web-app: full-screen big dialogs on mobile viewports
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Big dialogs (settings, about, gallery, profiles, new chat, QR scanner)
go edge-to-edge on phone-sized viewports instead of floating as small
rounded boxes, and the QR camera view fills the available height.

Keyed on each dialog's `data-testid` (attribute selectors stay global in
CSS modules), so no prop needs threading through <Dialog> and
<DialogWithHeader>: dialogs that already carry a testid need no diff at
all, the anonymous ones get a one-line `dataTestid`. The selector list
also pre-names dialogs opted in further down (connectivity, edit
profile, settings sections) and by desktop/1018 (public bots/channels) — unmatched attribute
selectors are inert, and those patches then stay one-liners too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

web-app: full-screen sub settings pages on mobile viewports

The above made the settings root dialog go edge to
edge on phones, but every page it opens on top still rendered as a small
floating dialog: the four settings sections (chats & media, notifications,
appearance, advanced), the connectivity view and the profile editor. Give
them the data-testids the fullscreen selector list already names, so
navigating through settings stays full-screen. Deeper pickers and alerts
(select dialogs, confirmations) intentionally stay small popups.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
